    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d391">

                <pb facs="0589" n="519" sameAs="frus:frus1919Parisv01/pg519"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">Paris Peace Conf. 185.111/28</note>
                <head>
                    <hi rendition="#italic">General Tasker H. Bliss to the Secretary of State </hi>
                </head>
                <opener>
                    <dateline rendition="#float-right">
                        <placeName>
                            <hi rendition="#small-caps">Paris</hi>
                        </placeName>, <date calendar="gregorian" when="1918-12-25">December 25,
                            1918</date>.</dateline>
                </opener>
                <p>
                    <hi rendition="#small-caps">My Dear Mr. Secretary</hi>: I send you herewith a
                    preliminary report on the subject of the League of Nations<anchor n="15"
                        xml:id="d391-f1"/> which, possibly, you <pb facs="0590" n="520"
                        xml:id="pg520"/> may find of some interest. The copy of the letter to me
                    from General Nolan,<anchor n="16" xml:id="d391-f2"/> which precedes the report,
                    will explain its origin.</p>
                <p>I received yesterday a second and fuller report, being an analysis of
                    propositions for a League of Nations and for Disarmament, which I am now having
                    copied and which I hope to be able to send to you before the end of the
                        week.<anchor n="17" xml:id="d391-f3"/>
                </p>
                <p>Cordially yours,</p>
                <closer>
                    <signed>
                        <hi rendition="#small-caps">Tasker H. Buss</hi>
                    </signed>
                </closer>


                <xi:include href="d391-a1.xml" xpointer="d391-a1"/>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
    <standOff>
        <listAnnotation>
